  "security_implications": "data_o normally outputs raw digest shares (potentially secret key material) when start && done_o is true; during other times a decoy value built from entropy_i is presented. The direct exposure of digest_share0/1 on data_o without additional masking assumes downstream consumers follow protocol and do not observe the bus during non-done windows. The width of DecoyOutputCopies must exactly match the digest-share width, otherwise bit-width mismatch could expose or truncate the decoy, weakening the masking property.",
